---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { getEntry } from 'astro:content';
const site = (await getEntry('site', 'site'))!.data;
---
<Base title="About" description="Brett Peterson: web developer, website owner, family man, BYU fan.">
  <section class="wrap pt-12">
    <h1 class="text-[clamp(4rem,13vw,11rem)] font-black uppercase">About</h1>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap mt-12 grid gap-16 lg:grid-cols-[2fr_1fr]">
    <div class="measure space-y-5 text-lg">
      <p>I'm Brett. I've been building for the web since 2009, starting with a services company I started with friends during the downturn and a long run of PHP, WordPress, Magento, and Joomla work.</p>
      <p>For almost seven years I owned getweave.com end to end: the code, the integrations, SEO and answer-engine strategy, competitor research, and the Salesforce lead routing that decided which leads reached sales. Along the way I turned website work into an engineering practice, with GitHub, CI/CD, and sprints for a marketing team.</p>
      <p>In September 2026 I joined Pattern. Most of what I build now is Next.js and Tailwind: client sites, small tools, and the games on this site.</p>
      <p>I live in {site.location} with my family. I'm good at explaining technical work to people who don't want to hear about technical work.</p>
    </div>
    <aside class="space-y-12">
      <figure class="border-l-2 border-royal pl-5">
        <blockquote class="font-display text-3xl font-bold leading-tight">“He is a tireless worker and fun co-worker to be around.”</blockquote>
        <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate">Dan, Leadgenix</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-4xl font-black">Gameday</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-slate">Lifelong BYU fan. The gameday anthem is still Fictionist's “Momentum.” Rise and shout.</p>
        <ul class="mt-4 space-y-1 text-sm">
          <li><a class="link" href="https://twitter.com/BYUCougars" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@BYUCougars</a></li>
          <li><a class="link" href="https://twitter.com/byuROC" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@byuROC, Roar of Cougars</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </section>
</Base>
